SM-T715 tablet: Wi-Fi passwords in WPA2-PSK when the radio has no SAE.

The tablet's BCM4358 firmware (brcmfmac, linux-firmware 7.112.300.14) has no
SAE, so a WPA3-Personal profile never associates ("association took too
long"), and the panel shows it as "Network out of range". Quickshell's
connectWithPsk writes key-mgmt=sae whenever the network it reports is SAE,
which happens for routers serving one SSID as WPA3 and as WPA2. The panel now asks `iw phy` once whether the radio names SAE;
without it, a password for an SAE network goes through nmcli with a WPA2-PSK
profile (key-mgmt pinned, password on stdin through `--ask`, as the upstream
fallback does; the SSID as a positional parameter; the profile deleted if it
fails to come up). With SAE, or without iw, nothing changes. Against
omarchy-mobile 87b8395 (omamobile-shell 0.2.94), packages/omamobile-shell
(applied with patch -p1 in that directory, after 0001).

diff --git a/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/WifiModel.js b/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/WifiModel.js
index ed8d2b3..1ae9cd8 100644
--- a/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/WifiModel.js
+++ b/plugins/omamobile.quicksettings/WifiModel.js
@@ -188,6 +188,29 @@ function nmcliConnectArgv(ssid, ifname) {
   return argv
 }
 
+// Whether `iw phy` says the radio can do SAE (WPA3-Personal): softMAC
+// drivers print "SAE with AUTHENTICATE", full-MAC ones list SAE_OFFLOAD.
+// The SM-T715's BCM4358 firmware has neither.
+function phyHasSae(iwPhy) {
+  return /\bSAE/.test(String(iwPhy || ""))
+}
+
+// Without SAE, a network Quickshell reports as SAE (in practice one SSID
+// served as WPA3 and WPA2) gets a WPA2-PSK profile through nmcli: Quickshell's
+// connectWithPsk would write key-mgmt=sae, which never associates. As in
+// nmcliConnectArgv the password is never an argument (`--ask` reads it from
+// stdin); the SSID and interface reach sh as positional parameters, never as
+// code. A profile that fails to come up is deleted, so a retry after a wrong
+// password doesn't leave a duplicate behind.
+function nmcliWpa2ConnectArgv(ssid, ifname) {
+  var script = 'u=$(cat /proc/sys/kernel/random/uuid) || exit; ' +
+    'nmcli connection add type wifi con-name "$1" ssid "$1" connection.uuid "$u" ' +
+    '${2:+ifname "$2"} wifi-sec.key-mgmt wpa-psk >/dev/null || exit; ' +
+    'nmcli --wait 45 --ask connection up uuid "$u" && exit; ' +
+    'rc=$?; nmcli connection delete uuid "$u" >/dev/null 2>&1; exit $rc'
+  return ["sh", "-c", script, "sh", String(ssid), String(ifname || "")]
+}
+
 function nmcliFailureMessage(stderr) {
   var text = String(stderr || "")
   if (/secrets were required|802-1x|psk|password|authentication/i.test(text)) return "Wrong password"
@@ -250,6 +273,8 @@ if (typeof module !== "undefined") {
     failureMessage: failureMessage,
     shouldReprompt: shouldReprompt,
     nmcliConnectArgv: nmcliConnectArgv,
+    phyHasSae: phyHasSae,
+    nmcliWpa2ConnectArgv: nmcliWpa2ConnectArgv,
     nmcliFailureMessage: nmcliFailureMessage,
     listEntries: listEntries,
     sameRows: sameRows
